{"id": "EUVD-2026-108755", "enisaUuid": "aef4dabf-9ea7-364e-a120-d17cf694aeb7", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nbtrfs: unlock inode and extent in caller when io_uring read extent fails\n\nbtrfs_uring_read_extent() runs only after btrfs_encoded_read() has taken\nthe inode shared lock and the extent lock.  On failure it used to unlock\nin out_fail, and a pages-array allocation failure returned -ENOMEM\nwithout unlocking at all.\n\nUnlock in the caller instead on all failure returns, matching the\ncopy_to_user() error path.  The deferred -EIOCBQUEUED path still unlocks\nin btrfs_uring_read_finished().", "datePublished": "2026-10-23T12:19:29", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-23T12:19:29", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/2797eb38773a96914ccedeec71eb2144645400b2", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/ada1fc725a4db407294ae90a0d40ef1c46f457f2", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/b6e8add5d79d1f6f819a054c833bab452bd7365d"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-98961"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.0, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "39da10e2-48a1-3fdc-b0c5-460e387b9c77", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "34310c442e175f286b4c06ab5caa4e0b267ea31c <ada1fc725a4db407294ae90a0d40ef1c46f457f2"}, {"id": "5b61c7c3-10ce-3c4e-be87-1aa83c461ed5", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "894806e7-17ae-389a-ad3d-801aca2d8a1c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "34310c442e175f286b4c06ab5caa4e0b267ea31c <2797eb38773a96914ccedeec71eb2144645400b2"}, {"id": "90ebe21e-08e7-3f34-8c0a-d626385f668e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.57"}, {"id": "9c3bb0a2-8472-3726-941b-4cefa2c9c10c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "34310c442e175f286b4c06ab5caa4e0b267ea31c <b6e8add5d79d1f6f819a054c833bab452bd7365d"}, {"id": "9ebab129-c352-3ea2-8329-d574f2cbe883", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.13"}, {"id": "ceac9e19-d0d6-35b9-8796-c693047322af", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.11"}, {"id": "e805c04d-c401-3458-8d71-9b9161ca269d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "86845b7d-da1c-3b7e-a74f-78c5ac09ca53", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}